{"kVec":{"title":"Vectors & dot product","mc":"#15803d","body":"<div class=\"m-meta\"><p class=\"role\">A list of numbers is a vector; the dot product <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\cdot b=\\sum_i a_i b_i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4445em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0497em;vertical-align:-0.2997em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop op-symbol small-op\" style=\"position:relative;top:0em;\">∑</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.162em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4003em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2997em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> measures how much two vectors point the same way.</p><div class=\"where\">📍 Location: <a data-go=\"T1\">App overview</a> › <a data-go=\"T2\">Agent</a> › <a data-go=\"T3\">LLM</a> › <a data-go=\"N\">Neural Network Basics</a> › <a data-go=\"K2\">Math · Linear algebra</a> › <b>Vectors &amp; dot product</b></div><span class=\"status no\">📐 Math foundation: not a component, but the rule behind the computation</span></div><div class=\"tryit\"><b>🧪 Try it: </b><button class=\"btn primary\" data-jump=\"labMat\" data-lv=\"K2\">🧪 Drag a 2×2 matrix (Linear algebra)</button></div><div class=\"m-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Card sections\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t0\" aria-controls=\"mt@p0\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">🎯 What it does</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t1\" aria-controls=\"mt@p1\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">▶ How to use</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t2\" aria-controls=\"mt@p2\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">🧠 Why</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t3\" aria-controls=\"mt@p3\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">⚠️ Limits</button></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p0\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t0\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"sec\"><h4>🎯 Role</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">∥</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">∥</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">∥</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">∥</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\cdot b=\\lVert a\\rVert\\,\\lVert b\\rVert\\cos\\theta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4445em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">∥</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mclose\">∥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">∥</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mclose\">∥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">cos</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span>: positive when aligned, 0 when perpendicular, negative when opposite.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p1\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t1\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec\" style=\"background:#f0f9ff\"><h4>▶ How to use it</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Word-vector similarity and the Q·K score in attention are both dot products.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p2\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t2\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p>A dot product is only multiply-adds, which hardware does extremely fast, and it has the geometric meaning of an angle.</p></div><div class=\"sec eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p>Proof on this stop: compare the law of cosines with the expansion of ‖a−b‖².</p></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p3\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t3\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><p class=\"lim\">⚠️ Limits / notes: The dot product depends on length; to compare direction only, use cosine similarity (divide by the lengths first).</p></div><!--m2pi--><div class=\"sn\"><p class=\"sn-h\"><span>🔤 Symbols used here</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-all\" data-sym=\"*\">📖 All symbols</button></p><ul class=\"sn-l\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>a</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “a”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">a vector (a list of numbers, drawn as an arrow)</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"cdot\">·</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “dot” (times)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">Another way to write times: 2·3 = 6. Between two lists of numbers (vectors) it is the “dot product”: multiply matching entries, then add them all up.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>b</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “b”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">another vector</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"sum\">Σ</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “sigma” (sum)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">“Add up a whole list.” Below: where to start; above: where to stop. With only a letter below, add over every possible value of it.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>i</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “i”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">a label: which one</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"sub\">□₁</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “sub” (the small lowered mark)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">A small lowered mark is a number or a label that tells apart several things of the same kind: label 1 and label 2 are the 1st one and the 2nd one.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"mul\">□□</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: no word: side by side means times</span><span class=\"sn-m\">Two things written right next to each other, with no sign between them, are multiplied: a number right before a letter means that number times it; two brackets side by side are multiplied.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"norm\">‖□‖</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “length” (norm)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">How long a vector (a list of numbers, drawn as an arrow) is. (3, 4) has length 5, since 3×3 + 4×4 = 25 = 5×5.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"cos\">cos</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “cosine”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">A number that depends on an angle, between −1 and 1. Pointing the same way gives 1, at right angles 0, opposite ways −1.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"theta\">θ</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “theta”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the angle between the two arrows</span></li></ul></div><!--/m2pi-->"},"kMat":{"title":"Matrix multiplication","mc":"#15803d","body":"<div class=\"m-meta\"><p class=\"role\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(AB)_{ij}=\\sum_k A_{ik}B_{kj}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0572em;\">ij</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0497em;vertical-align:-0.2997em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop op-symbol small-op\" style=\"position:relative;top:0em;\">∑</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1864em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4003em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2997em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">ik</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0502em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0572em;\">j</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: the dot product of row i with column j.</p><div class=\"where\">📍 Location: <a data-go=\"T1\">App overview</a> › <a data-go=\"T2\">Agent</a> › <a data-go=\"T3\">LLM</a> › <a data-go=\"N\">Neural Network Basics</a> › <a data-go=\"K2\">Math · Linear algebra</a> › <b>Matrix multiplication</b></div><span class=\"status no\">📐 Math foundation: not a component, but the rule behind the computation</span></div><div class=\"tryit\"><b>🧪 Try it: </b><button class=\"btn primary\" data-jump=\"labMat\" data-lv=\"K2\">🧪 Drag a 2×2 matrix (Linear algebra)</button></div><div class=\"m-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Card sections\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t0\" aria-controls=\"mt@p0\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">🎯 What it does</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t1\" aria-controls=\"mt@p1\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">▶ How to use</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t2\" aria-controls=\"mt@p2\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">🧠 Why</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t3\" aria-controls=\"mt@p3\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">⚠️ Limits</button></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p0\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t0\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"sec\"><h4>🎯 Role</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>A fully connected layer is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=Wx+b</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span></span></span></span>; a matrix maps one vector to another (a linear map).</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p1\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t1\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec\" style=\"background:#f0f9ff\"><h4>▶ How to use it</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Shape rule: (m×n)(n×p) = m×p; the inner n must match.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p2\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t2\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p>Batching many dot products into one matrix multiplication lets a GPU compute them in parallel; most of an LLM’s compute is matrix multiplication.</p></div><div class=\"sec eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p>(m×n)(n×p) takes m·n·p multiply-adds, so the cost is known in advance.</p></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p3\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t3\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><p class=\"lim\">⚠️ Limits / notes: In general AB ≠ BA; the order matters.</p></div><!--m2pi--><div class=\"sn\"><p class=\"sn-h\"><span>🔤 Symbols used here</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-all\" data-sym=\"*\">📖 All symbols</button></p><ul class=\"sn-l\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>A</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “A”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the first table of numbers (matrix)</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"mul\">□□</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: no word: side by side means times</span><span class=\"sn-m\">Two things written right next to each other, with no sign between them, are multiplied: a number right before a letter means that number times it; two brackets side by side are multiplied.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>B</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “B”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the second table of numbers (matrix)</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"sub\">□₁</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “sub” (the small lowered mark)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">A small lowered mark is a number or a label that tells apart several things of the same kind: label 1 and label 2 are the 1st one and the 2nd one.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>i</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “i”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">which row</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>j</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “j”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">which column</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"sum\">Σ</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “sigma” (sum)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">“Add up a whole list.” Below: where to start; above: where to stop. With only a letter below, add over every possible value of it.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>k</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “k”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the counting label in the sum: pairs up A’s row with B’s column, one by one</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>y</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “y”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the output list</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>W</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “W”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the weight matrix: a table of numbers that gets learned</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>x</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “x”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the input list</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>b</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “b”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the bias: a list added at the end</span></li></ul></div><!--/m2pi-->"},"kDet":{"title":"Linear maps & determinant","mc":"#15803d","body":"<div class=\"m-meta\"><p class=\"role\">A 2×2 matrix turns the unit square into a parallelogram whose area is multiplied by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>det</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|\\det A|=|ad-bc|</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">det</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span></span></span></span>.</p><div class=\"where\">📍 Location: <a data-go=\"T1\">App overview</a> › <a data-go=\"T2\">Agent</a> › <a data-go=\"T3\">LLM</a> › <a data-go=\"N\">Neural Network Basics</a> › <a data-go=\"K2\">Math · Linear algebra</a> › <b>Linear maps &amp; determinant</b></div><span class=\"status no\">📐 Math foundation: not a component, but the rule behind the computation</span></div><div class=\"tryit\"><b>🧪 Try it: </b><button class=\"btn primary\" data-jump=\"labMat\" data-lv=\"K2\">🧪 Drag a 2×2 matrix (Linear algebra)</button></div><div class=\"m-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Card sections\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t0\" aria-controls=\"mt@p0\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">🎯 What it does</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t1\" aria-controls=\"mt@p1\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">▶ How to use</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t2\" aria-controls=\"mt@p2\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">🧠 Why</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t3\" aria-controls=\"mt@p3\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">⚠️ Limits</button></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p0\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t0\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"sec\"><h4>🎯 Role</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Determinant 0: the plane is squashed onto a line (or a point); information is lost and the matrix has no inverse.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p1\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t1\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec\" style=\"background:#f0f9ff\"><h4>▶ How to use it</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Drag the four numbers in the lab and watch the square stretch, rotate and flip.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p2\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t2\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p>The two columns are where the two basis vectors land; the whole plane follows them.</p></div><div class=\"sec eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p>This one intuition, “look at the columns”, explains what any 2×2 matrix does.</p></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p3\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t3\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><p class=\"lim\">⚠️ Limits / notes: In high dimensions it cannot be drawn, but “the columns are where the basis vectors go” still holds.</p></div><!--m2pi--><div class=\"sn\"><p class=\"sn-h\"><span>🔤 Symbols used here</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-all\" data-sym=\"*\">📖 All symbols</button></p><ul class=\"sn-l\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"abs\">|□|</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “absolute value”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">Drop the plus or minus sign and keep the size: how far from 0. |−3| = 3, |3| = 3. The absolute value of a difference is the distance between the two numbers.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"det\">det</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “determinant”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">How many times a matrix scales area. Negative means the shape was flipped over; 0 means it was squashed flat onto a line (or a point).</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>A</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “A”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">a 2×2 matrix: the rule that moves every point on the sheet</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>a</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “a”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the top-left number of the matrix</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"mul\">□□</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: no word: side by side means times</span><span class=\"sn-m\">Two things written right next to each other, with no sign between them, are multiplied: a number right before a letter means that number times it; two brackets side by side are multiplied.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>d</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “d”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the bottom-right number of the matrix</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>b</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “b”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the top-right number of the matrix</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>c</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “c”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the bottom-left number of the matrix</span></li></ul></div><!--/m2pi-->"},"kJac":{"title":"Transpose & Jacobian","mc":"#15803d","body":"<div class=\"m-meta\"><p class=\"role\">The matrix of all partial derivatives of a vector function, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∂</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∂</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J_{ij}=\\partial y_i/\\partial x_j</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0962em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0572em;\">ij</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"margin-right:0.0556em;\">∂</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"margin-right:0.0556em;\">∂</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0572em;\">j</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>; gradients flow back through its transpose.</p><div class=\"where\">📍 Location: <a data-go=\"T1\">App overview</a> › <a data-go=\"T2\">Agent</a> › <a data-go=\"T3\">LLM</a> › <a data-go=\"N\">Neural Network Basics</a> › <a data-go=\"K2\">Math · Linear algebra</a> › <b>Transpose &amp; Jacobian</b></div><span class=\"status no\">📐 Math foundation: not a component, but the rule behind the computation</span></div><div class=\"tryit\"><b>🧪 Try it: </b><button class=\"btn primary\" data-jump=\"labGradCheck\" data-lv=\"K5\">🧪 Backprop vs numerical gradient (Derivations)</button></div><div class=\"m-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Card sections\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t0\" aria-controls=\"mt@p0\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">🎯 What it does</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t1\" aria-controls=\"mt@p1\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">▶ How to use</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t2\" aria-controls=\"mt@p2\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">🧠 Why</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t3\" aria-controls=\"mt@p3\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">⚠️ Limits</button></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p0\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t0\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"sec\"><h4>🎯 Role</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>For <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=Wx</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span> the Jacobian is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span></span></span></span>, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∇</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">⊤</mi></msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∇</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla_x L=W^{\\top}\\nabla_y L</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">∇</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.1352em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">⊤</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">∇</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span>.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p1\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t1\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec\" style=\"background:#f0f9ff\"><h4>▶ How to use it</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Every layer in backpropagation does exactly this “multiply by the transpose”.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p2\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t2\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p>In many dimensions the chain rule becomes a product of Jacobians.</p></div><div class=\"sec eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p>Only “Jacobian-transpose times a vector” is needed; the huge Jacobian is never stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p3\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t3\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><p class=\"lim\">⚠️ Limits / notes: The proofs here use index sums only, no tensor notation.</p></div><!--m2pi--><div class=\"sn\"><p class=\"sn-h\"><span>🔤 Symbols used here</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-all\" data-sym=\"*\">📖 All symbols</button></p><ul class=\"sn-l\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>J</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “J”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the Jacobian: the table of how sensitive each output is to each input</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"sub\">□₁</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “sub” (the small lowered mark)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">A small lowered mark is a number or a label that tells apart several things of the same kind: label 1 and label 2 are the 1st one and the 2nd one.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>i</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “i”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">which output</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>j</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “j”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">which input</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"partial\">∂</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “partial” (or “del”)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">The partial-derivative sign: keep every other input still, move just one a tiny bit, and see how fast the result changes.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>y</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “y”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the layer’s output list</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"slash\">/</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “divided by” (slash)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">Another way to write division: 6/3 means 6÷3 = 2.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>x</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “x”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the layer’s input list</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>W</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “W”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the weight matrix: a table of numbers that gets learned</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"mul\">□□</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: no word: side by side means times</span><span class=\"sn-m\">Two things written right next to each other, with no sign between them, are multiplied: a number right before a letter means that number times it; two brackets side by side are multiplied.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"nabla\">∇</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “nabla” or “del”: the gradient</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the gradient: how sensitive the loss is to each input (or weight), as a list</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>L</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “L”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the loss: how wrong the model is</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"T\">□ᵀ</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “transpose”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">Flip a table of numbers over its diagonal: row 1 becomes column 1, row 2 becomes column 2, and so on.</span></li></ul></div><!--/m2pi-->"}}
